# Lifeline (prototype)

Medical-records prototype on Supabase Auth + Postgres. Use fictional data only. Not security-reviewed.

## Run locally
    npm install
    npm run dev

## Set up Supabase (once)
1. SQL Editor: paste `sql/lifeline_supabase_ALL.sql` into an empty tab and Run.
2. Authentication -> Providers -> Email: on. Turn "Confirm email" off while testing.
3. Authentication -> URL Configuration: set Site URL to your hosted address and add `<address>/login` as a Redirect URL.

## Deploy (Netlify or Vercel, from GitHub)
Build command `npm run build`, output folder `dist`.
Environment variables (optional, defaults are built in): `VITE_SUPABASE_URL`, `VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY`.
Never add a service_role or secret key anywhere in this project.
